# The `caos-test-result` tool (SPEC, "Tools"): the std/bash worker image with
# this directory's script curried onto it, plus the `help` the agent registers
# it by. It moved out of caos-tools/ into std/ alongside caos-test so the agent
# harness DEPends on it and offers it ALWAYS (design/flake-inputs.md, "the tui").
# Unlike caos-build/caos-test it reads a record BY HASH and touches no workspace,
# so it needs no wrong-tree guard and runs on plain std/bash.
#
# The docs are a HERE-STRING, so they live in the `.caos-expr` — which is
# STRIPPED from the tree the expression is evaluated against. Editing them
# re-keys this tool's arg tree and nothing else: no build sees these bytes.
HELP=<<END
Print one test's COMPLETE record from a `caos-test` run: the test's whole output —
the report only carries its last few lines — or, with `log`, one of the inner
stack's logs. Takes the hash the caos-test report prints beside each test's name;
that hash is stable, so the record of a run stays readable long after the run.
@param hash The hash the `caos-test` report prints beside a test's name.
@param [log] Print this inner-stack log instead of the test's output: server, runnerd, redis or serve.
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/bash --worker1:@=worker.sh --help=$HELP
